        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(infra): consolidate retry scheduling",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCore infrastructure and the memory host SDK carried separate retry implementations. The memory fork predated the canonical Retry-After floor fix in #68543 and retained rounded, symmetric jitter, so fractional server hints could be scheduled below the requested floor.\n\nCloses #105757.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Adds a dependency-free `@openclaw/retry` leaf package for retry scheduling and policy.\n- Keeps core-only attempt diagnostics in the thin `src/infra/retry.ts` adapter.\n- Replaces the memory-host fork and the bounded ClawHub, QQBot, cron delivery, and media-store retry loops with the shared implementation.\n- Keeps QQBot's deadline-driven persistent loop local because it is not a bounded retry policy.\n- Preserves caller-specific schedules, retry predicates, abort handling, final-response behavior, and logging.\n- Tests Retry-After floors with zero and positive jitter, timer clamping, error identity, caller schedules, and migrated behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRetry-After values are now treated consistently across these paths and are never rounded below the server-provided floor. Existing retry counts and backoff schedules remain unchanged; duplicated policy code is removed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox focused suite: shared retry package, core retry, memory host, ClawHub, cron delivery, media store, QQBot, and Vitest alias tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox full `pnpm build` passed, including package/declaration graph and SDK declaration budget.\n- Blacksmith Testbox changed checks passed formatting, package/API/storage gates, and all typecheck lanes; scoped lint and tests passed after a mechanical test-style cleanup.\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted or actionable findings.\n\n",
        "branch": "codex/consolidate-retry-backoff",
